blurb: The school board approved the superintendent's contract and then engaged in
  a contentious debate over Kaler Elementary student attendance zones, ultimately
  passing the administration's proposal after an initial tie vote and reconsideration,
  with a strong emphasis on prioritizing Kaler families in the waiver and transportation
  processes. The meeting also highlighted staff resignations and community concerns
  regarding communication and the emotional toll of school changes.
